  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 233 AM MDT Thu Apr 23 2026\n\nToday through Sat Night. As the wet low of yesterday exits, yet\nanother, drier but colder, low moves in from the north. It will\nproduce only light precipitation, but the snow levels will be \nlower and the very strong west northwesterly wind means that the\neastern Magic Valley will reach Wind Advisory conditions. The \ncurrent Winter Weather Advisories appear on schedule to expire \nat their current expiration times, later this morning and this \nevening. Fri night and Sat will see very little precipitation,\nlimited to high elevations, but then Sat night will see a return\nof moisture mainly to the northern half of the mountains and\nhighlands. Precipitation appears to continue light with inland\nCanada still being the source of the air mass. \n\nAs expected, this second low will bring in cold air, plunging\novernight lows in a large portion of the Snake River plain and\neastern Magic Valley into a freeze. However, the portions that\nare not affected includes the highway corridor from Idaho Falls\nthrough Pocatello to Burley. Fri night appears to be even colder\nand all but the Burley-Richfield area are affected. Afternoon\nhighs bottom out Fri and a warming trend develops Sat, but\ntemperatures will only warm into the 50s, maybe 60 in the\nsouthern Magic Valley. \n\nThe support for west wind aloft will push wind in the eastern\nMagic Valley to Wind Advisory conditions with gusts up to 50 mph\nexpected for a short interval from mid-afternoon to early\nevening today. The wind is not expected to repeat to this level\non Fri or Sat, with a gradual decrease in the wind from day to\nday. \n\nSun through Wed. Cluster analysis indicates a solid chance of\nSun and Mon remaining wet and colder than normal, then a\npossible transition to drier weather Tue and Wed. Tue and Wed\nhave temperatures close to climatic averages for the time of\nyear and below average risk of precipitation. About 70 percent\nof the cluster solutions for Tue and Wed are for a dry period.",
